--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INDICATOR DATA IS LICENSED SEPARATELY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The indicator set in iocs/ is NOT covered by the Apache License above. It is
released into the public domain under CC0 1.0 so that it can be copied into
blocklists, STIX bundles, MISP instances and other tools without friction.
See iocs/LICENSE.md.

iocs/curated_targeted.txt holds file fingerprints and package names copied from
researchers' own indicator files. The selection is CC0; the values remain under
their publishers' terms where those apply, and each notice is kept in that file's
header: ESET and Volexity (BSD-2-Clause), Meta and Palo Alto Networks Unit 42
(MIT), Lookout (Apache License 2.0), Amnesty International (CC BY 2.0) and Cisco
Talos (CC0).

The optional Candiru YARA rules are NOT part of that CC0 indicator grant.
Microsoft Threat Intelligence Center's MAL_DevilsTongue_HijackDll rule is
redistributed from Signature-Base under Detection Rule License 1.1.
Felix Bilstein's win_devilstongue_auto rule is redistributed from Malpedia
under CC BY-SA 4.0. Both rules are unchanged. Author, source and license
attribution are retained in the embedded rules, match details, and
third_party/candiru/. YARA-X itself is a separate optional BSD-3-Clause
dependency, not embedded executable code in this script.

Primary sources for the indicator set:

  The Citizen Lab, "Exposing AdFection: How Discover-Tech Turned Targeted Ads
  Into a Pipeline for Zero-Click Mercenary Spyware", 2026-10-15.

  Recorded Future / Insikt Group, "Devil's Tongue" infrastructure reporting,
  CTA-2025-0805, August 2025.

  Additional Candiru research from The Citizen Lab (2021, 2022), Confiant
  (2026), Microsoft (2021), ESET (2021), Avast / Gen (2022), Google Threat
  Analysis Group (2021) and Amnesty International Security Lab (2024).
  Full report titles, dates and links: iocs/LICENSE.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS SOFTWARE DOES NOT PROMISE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A result of "no known indicators found" is not a clean bill of health, and this
software states so in its own output. It cannot detect an unknown indicator, it
cannot see evidence that has already expired, and it is not a substitute for
expert forensic help. Anyone with real reason for concern should contact the
Access Now Digital Security Helpline (https://www.accessnow.org/help/) or the
Amnesty International Security Lab (https://securitylab.amnesty.org/).
